==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthorisationEnforced  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuthorisationEnforced.als
    rationale: Removing the constraint that Permitted outcomes require an allowed (Relationship, OperationKind) cell lets Alloy construct a world where, e.g., a NonCTClinician receives Permitted on GetRecord, directly violating LeastPrivilege and FR_004_CareTeamGating.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_004_CareTeamGating, FR_006_PatientSelfAccess, FR_007_ComplianceOfficerDeniedClinicalContent
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_006_PatientSelfAccess: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_007_ComplianceOfficerDeniedClinicalContent: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditEntryBijection  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditEntryBijection.als
    rationale: Removing the bijection between Operations and AuditEntries allows Alloy to place two Operations sharing one AuditEntry, violating the one-entry-per-access invariant of FR-013, or to have an AuditEntry with no corresponding Operation, violating SC-002.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_013_AlwaysOnAudit, AppendOnly
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing the fact that pins an AuditEntry's outcome to its Operation's outcome lets Alloy construct a world where an entry's entryOutcome differs from the operation that produced it — a direct mutation of an immutable field, violating FR-015.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_015_AuditImmutability
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutability: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_NoteAuthorIsActiveCareteamClinician  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteAuthorIsActiveCareteamClinician.als
    rationale: Removing the care-team constraint on note authorship allows Alloy to produce a ClinicalNote authored by a non-clinician or a clinician not on the care team, violating FR-012 and the LeastPrivilege property for PostNote.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NotesAppendOnly, AppendOnly, LeastPrivilege
      - FR_012_NotesAppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_PatientRecordExclusivity  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PatientRecordExclusivity.als
    rationale: Removing the constraint that no two patients share an assigned record allows Alloy to place two Patient users pointing at the same Record, collapsing the ownership model and invalidating the basis for OwnershipBasedAccess assertions.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_003_PatientAssignedRecord: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the closed-world assignment of PermMatrix.Allowed lets Alloy add extra cells — e.g., ComplianceRel->GetRecord — which directly violates FR-007 (compliance content-blindness) and PermissionGrounding (no silent grants), and breaks PermissionCompleteness because the cell count would differ from 7.
    expected to FAIL: PermissionCompleteness, PermissionGrounding, FR_007_ComplianceOfficerDeniedClinicalContent, FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceOfficerDeniedClinicalContent: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AccessLogComplianceOnly: FAIL (expected)

